<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<opml version="2.0"><head><title>Playing Ironsworn in Pointliner</title></head><body>
<outline text="# Playing Ironsworn in Pointliner">
  <outline text="Ironsworn's system wired into Pointliner pills: action rolls, momentum, progress tracks, and oracles, all live in one file. See ironsworn.md for the walkthrough. The dice, tracking and oracle pills are complete; the moves are marked slots for the SRD's own text, and the oracles carry filler you replace with the SRD's entries. Every pill here is live, click one to run it."/>
  <outline text="Adapted from the Ironsworn System Reference Document by Shawn Tomkin, used under CC BY 4.0 (creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0). Changes made: the moves and oracle tables are restructured into outline points and pills. This adaptation is offered under the same CC BY 4.0 terms, separate from Pointliner's AGPLv3 app licence. Ironsworn is named descriptively; no logo or art is reproduced.">
    <outline text="Each move below is a marked slot for its SRD text, and the oracles hold filler options written for this demo. Paste each move's text into its slot, and replace the filler inside each `{rule ...}` with that oracle's entries; every pill is already wired, so an oracle updates the moment you edit its rule."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## The action roll">
    <outline text="Roll the action die and stat, then two challenge dice. Beat both = strong hit, one = weak hit, neither = miss. Edit the +2 to your stat plus any adds."/>
    <outline text="Action die + stat: {1d6+2}"/>
    <outline text="Challenge dice (rolled together): {2x: {1d10}}"/>
    <outline text="Or roll the challenge dice one at a time: {1d10} and {1d10}"/>
    <outline text="Put a stat in a variable so every roll reads it: {edge := 2}"/>
    <outline text="Face danger with Edge: {1d6} + {edge} against {1d10} and {1d10}. Change edge above and every roll that reads it updates."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Momentum">
    <outline text="Momentum is the swing resource. Track it here and edit as it rises and falls; burn it by reading this value against the challenge dice you rolled."/>
    <outline text="Current momentum: {momentum := 2}"/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Progress tracks">
    <outline text="A vow, journey, or fight is a progress cookie over ten boxes. Check boxes as you advance; when it is time, count the filled boxes and roll the challenge dice against that number.">
      <outline text="Swear an iron vow: reach the drowned tower [/]">
        <outline text="- [x] box"/>
        <outline text="- [x] box"/>
        <outline text="- [x] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
        <outline text="- [ ] box"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Progress move when ready: roll {1d10} and {1d10} against the number of filled boxes above."/>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Oracles">
    <outline text="An oracle table is a weighted pick. Declare each with the rule keyword, as `{rule name: option | option}`, then call it by name anywhere. A bare `name: option | option` is ordinary text and registers nothing. Replace the filler options with the SRD's entries, separated by | bars."/>
    <outline text="{rule action_oracle: strike | avenge | uncover | defend}"/>
    <outline text="{rule theme_oracle: risk | fortune | secret | shelter}"/>
    <outline text="Action plus Theme spark (two words): {action_oracle} {theme_oracle}"/>
    <outline text="Ask yes or no at even odds: {Yes 1 | No 1}. For other likelihoods, set the weights to the SRD odds (a likely question might be {Yes 3 | No 1})."/>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Moves">
    <outline text="Each move is its own point: the SRD trigger and strong/weak/miss outcomes sit in the point, with an action-roll pill ready beneath it. Play a move by reading its trigger, rolling, and reading the outcome for your result.">
      <outline text="Face Danger (SLOT: paste this move's trigger and strong/weak/miss text from the SRD)">
        <outline text="Roll: {1d6} + {edge} against {1d10} and {1d10}"/>
      </outline>
      <outline text="Secure an Advantage (SLOT: paste this move's text from the SRD)">
        <outline text="Roll: {1d6+2} against {1d10} and {1d10}"/>
      </outline>
    </outline>
  </outline>
  <outline text="## Run it yourself">
    <outline text="Click the action and challenge pills to roll a move. Check a progress box, then roll against the track when it fills. Click an oracle pill for a result, then swap its filler for the SRD's own entries. Edit momentum and edge as they change. Add the moves and oracles you use most, and it is your Ironsworn table."/>
  </outline>
</outline>
</body></opml>
